course: dictionary
lesson: 7112
title: Peculiarly: strange, special, or only found in one place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peculiarly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how something is. It comes from the word peculiar, and the -ly ending is a clue that it describes the way something is done.
explain: Most often it means in a strange or odd way. Tortoise calls putting his hind legs round his ears «so peculiarly comfortable», and we know that is an odd thing to do, even though he finds it comfortable.
explain: Sometimes it means especially or particularly, as in «peculiarly difficult», which means particularly hard. It can also mean belonging only to one group or place, as in «peculiarly British», which means typical of Britain only.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Oddly comfortable» works for Tortoise, «particularly difficult» works for a hard task, and «only British» works for a British custom.
fact: Peculiarly is an adverb, and it describes how something is or how something happens.
fact: «Peculiarly» means in a strange or odd way.
fact: «Peculiarly» can also mean especially or particularly, as in «peculiarly difficult».
fact: «Peculiarly British» means typical of Britain only, belonging to one place.
fact: Use the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits best.
exercise: What does peculiarly mean in «so peculiarly comfortable»? | Quickly and quietly | Very loudly | *In a strange or odd way | Sadly
exercise: A puzzle is «peculiarly difficult». What does peculiarly mean here? | Oddly and strangely | Quickly and easily | *Especially, or particularly | Only in one place
exercise: What does «peculiarly British» mean? | Written in French | *Typical of Britain only | Very kind to visitors | Found in every country
test: What kind of word is peculiarly? | *An adverb | A noun | A verb | A colour
test: In «a peculiarly British custom», what does peculiarly show? | *That the custom belongs only to Britain | That the custom is very loud | That the custom is brand new | That the custom is a kind of food
exam: Tortoise says putting his legs round his ears is «so peculiarly comfortable». What do we learn? | It hurts him badly | *It is strange, yet he finds it comfortable | It is a common thing everyone does | He is feeling cold
